'' RUN: std/chrono MonthName / WeekdayName follow the OS locale (GetLocaleInfoEx on
'' Windows, compared with an independent read; on Linux a private LC_TIME newlocale, so
'' LC_ALL=de_DE.UTF-8 gives "März" and LC_ALL=C "March" -- that half is run there by hand).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/chrono-locale-names.tiko -o tests/codegen/chronolocnames.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/chronolocnames.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/chronolocnames.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ok
